# core.autocrlf=true on this machine rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. That is fine for
# Python and TypeScript; it is fatal for a shell script that runs inside a Linux
# container, where `sh` reads the trailing \r as part of the command and the release
# fails to start. These files stay LF in the working tree no matter whose machine it is.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
